# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Device Port Reporter — restricted-data safeguards.
#
# Customer policy: no customer-supplied running-config, parsed report,
# or exported XLSX may ever be committed to the repo. These patterns
# block the common ways such files could sneak in — files a user might
# drag into the project, test outputs written by the CLI, or server
# logs that might capture diagnostics.
#
# The ONLY intentionally-tracked user-ish file is example_show_run.txt,
# which is a synthetic sample (no real device data). It is re-allowed
# at the bottom of this block.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
**/*.xlsx
**/*.xls
**/*.csv
**/*.cfg
**/*.conf
**/*.nxos
**/*.ios
**/*.log
**/*.err
**/*show*run*.txt
**/*show-run*.txt
**/*show_run*.txt
**/*running-config*.txt
**/*running_config*.txt
uploads/
output/
tmp/
web/uploads/
web/output/
web/tmp/

# Explicitly re-allow the synthetic sample (safe to ship).
!example_show_run.txt
